Organizations **rarely share the same governance model**. A professional body may run elections across multiple constituencies. A federation may assign different voting weights to its members. A cooperative may require delegation to ensure representation in large assemblies.

These processes are common in statutory governance, but they are often difficult to support with standard voting platforms, forcing organizations to rely on manual processes or cumbersome user interfaces.

With [**Vocdoni App**](https://app.vocdoni.io) **2.3**, we are extending our SaaS voting platform to support these governance structures more directly. This release focuses on **enabling weighted voting, delegation and hybrid voting workflows** in a way that remains verifiable and manageable through the platform interface.

### **What Vocdoni App already provides**

[**_Vocdoni App_**](https://app.vocdoni.io) is a digital voting platform designed for organizations that need **verifiable decision-making with guarantees, regulatory compliance and user-friendly experience**. Covering most types of online voting use cases for all kinds of organizations.

## **What’s new in Vocdoni App 2.3**

Version 2.3 focuses on enabling governance teams to manage more complex statutory voting requirements directly within the platform. Let’s dive into the new features:

### **Improved support for weighted voting processes**

Many formal governance structures **require voting rights to reflect weights** rather than a one-person-one-vote model. This is common in:

- Shareholder meetings
- Annual General Meetings (AGMs)
- Federations with differentiated representation
- Cooperatives with specific voting rights

![Vocdoni members table with columns for first name, last name, phone, member number and a highlighted voting power column holding the weights 80, 80, 20 and 20.](/blog/images/2026/02/vocdoni_weighted_voting-1.webp)

You can now adjust individual user voting weights directly in the UI, and also import weight data uploading a spreadsheet.

Vocdoni App 2.3 strengthens support for these scenarios and makes **weighted voting easier to manage through the platform interface**. This allows organizations to run votes that accurately reflect their governance rules, without requiring manual reconciliation after the vote.

### **Vote delegation support**

**Delegation is a common requirement** in many governance frameworks, where members are allowed to vote through authorized representatives. These systems usually follow either an **imperative mandate** (where the delegate must vote according to the member’s explicit instructions) or a **representative mandate** (where the delegate votes at their own discretion). This is particularly relevant for large cooperatives, professional bodies, and institutional membership organizations where direct participation is not always possible.

Vocdoni App 2.3 adds **support for representative mandate**, one of the most widely used delegation models. This use case is fully operational, leverages our weighted voting capabilities, and a dedicated delegation workflow will be introduced in a future update.

### **Hybrid voting and much more with live censuses**

Vocdoni App 2.3 introduces **Live Censuses**, allowing administrators to **manage voter eligibility and credentials** during an **active voting process**.

Administrators can now:

- Edit voter credentials while a vote is live,
- Remove eligible voters from the census during an ongoing process.

This provides greater operational control in real governance scenarios, particularly where **errors must be corrected** immediately or where **hybrid voting** is required.

For example, in **hybrid AGMs combining paper and digital voting**, Live Censuses allow administrators to remove digital voting access for participants who have already voted in person, reducing the risk of duplicate voting and improving process consistency.

![Edit member dialog with fields for first name, last name, email, phone, member number, national ID and birth date, closing with a voting power stepper set to 20 above the cancel and save changes buttons.](/blog/images/2026/02/vocdoni_edit_member.webp)

You can edit or remove voter data at any time, and changes are reflected instantly in ongoing voting processes.

## **Additional improvements in 2.3**

In addition to the governance-related features above, Vocdoni App 2.3 includes several improvements aimed at simplifying administration and access.

### **Google Sign-on**

Vocdoni App 2.3 adds **Google Sign-on**, including the ability to link an existing Vocdoni account to a Google account.

### **Plan usage visibility**

This release improves **visibility into plan usage**, helping organizations track current consumption and anticipate plan limits more clearly.

![Plan usage panel with three progress bars: 3 of 5 voting processes, 11 of 100 on memberbase size, and 2 of 100 two-factor email codes.](/blog/images/2026/02/vocdoni_usage_plan.webp)

Monitor your plan usage directly from your dashboard and receive alerts as you near or exceed your limits.

### **Italian language support**

Vocdoni App 2.3 adds **Italian localization**, expanding accessibility for organizations operating in Italian-speaking regions. The [_Associazione Termotecnica Italiana_](https://www.atinazionale.it) (Sezione Friuli Venezia Giulia) has already used it in their latest AGM, and we thank them for their collaboration in reviewing and validating the translation to ensure clarity and accuracy for Italian-speaking users.

## **Closer to meeting the governance needs of any organization**

With this version, Vocdoni App moves closer to **supporting the needs of any organization**, professional association, federation, cooperative, company, trade union, and public institution through a **verifiable**, **secure**, **privacy-centric** and **fully self-service** platform.

We cover most of the needs, but for organizations requiring **tailored workflows**, custom configurations, or **additional support**, the Vocdoni team can provide [_dedicated assistance_](https://vocdoni.io/contact).

## **Roadmap**

Following this release, **upcoming improvements** include:

- Platform modernization (Server Side Rendering and Chakra v3)
- PDF report generation for election results to support audit workflows
- More flexible pricing options
- Greek localization

### **FAQs**

#### **Is Vocdoni App compliant with GDPR?**

Yes. **Vocdoni App is fully GDPR compliant** and designed with privacy by default. The platform follows strict data protection principles and **data minimization** to ensure that personal data is handled securely and in accordance with European data protection regulations.

#### **Is Vocdoni App aligned with regulatory and statutory frameworks?**

Yes. Vocdoni App is designed to **meet the requirements of multiple legal and regulatory frameworks**, as well as the internal statutes and governance rules of most organizations.

#### **Is Vocdoni secure?**

Yes. Vocdoni App runs on the Vocdoni open-source voting protocol, which is built to provide **secure**, **end-to-end verifiable**, and **privacy-first voting**. The protocol is designed to ensure integrity, auditability, and resistance to manipulation. For many organizations, using a secure and verifiable voting system is not only best practice but **a regulatory requirement, and it significantly reduces the risk of disputes or challenges to the validity of results**.

